{
  "id": "sixth-sense",
  "term": "sixth sense",
  "definition": "In this historical source, “sixth sense” refers to common bodily feeling or general sensation: an overall sense of bodily lightness and liveliness, or of tiredness and weariness, arising apart from work or illness. It is used as another name for coenesthesis.",
